When editing Python source:

- `from __future__ import annotations` at the top; prefer modern typing.
- One primary class/model per file; keep modules focused.
- Keep heavy/optional imports lazy (inside functions) when a module must import
  without the optional dependency present.
- Public functions get docstrings; resolvers/handlers degrade gracefully at
  trust boundaries rather than raising 500s.
